From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a profile's Global Privacy Control reaches its
 pages

A desk's profile asks sites not to sell or share its data unless its
config's `protections.global_privacy_control` is off. Chrome has the
signal (`Sec-GPC: 1` and `navigator.globalPrivacyControl`) and reads it
from universal_optout's pref, but only while kUniversalOptOutSettings is
on, and it is off by default.

kUniversalOptOutSettings is on. ApplyProtections sets the pref per
profile; guard-browser-protections.sh checks it.
---
 components/universal_optout/features.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/universal_optout/features.cc b/components/universal_optout/features.cc
index a31476e..84f0c50 100644
--- a/components/universal_optout/features.cc
+++ b/components/universal_optout/features.cc
@@ -26,7 +26,9 @@ BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutExtension, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutExtensionSilent,
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
-BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutSettings, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+// Domicile: on. A profile's `protections.global_privacy_control` sets
+// kUniversalOptOutEnabled, which only reaches pages while this is on.
+BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutSettings, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kUniversalOptOutUpdateOnGeoLocationChanged,
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
